---
// About, concept: a first-person narrative drafted from Saad's share-safe handoff (career history and ways of
// working, generalised, no employer or product names). Every sentence is for Saad to correct before publication.
import ConceptLayout from '../../layouts/ConceptLayout.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../../data/site';
import { url } from '../../utils/url';
---

<ConceptLayout title="About" label="shared page for A, B and C (draft copy for Saad to correct)" current="about">
  <article class="container-wide about-c" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <header class="about-c__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 id="about-title">Hello, I'm Saad.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I'm a data engineer in London. I build and run the data platforms that reporting, CRM and analytics depend on,
        currently in the online gaming industry.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="about-c__body">
      <section aria-labelledby="work">
        <h2 id="work">The problems I work on</h2>
        <p>
          Most of my work sits where data moves between systems: capturing changes from operational databases, modelling
          them in a warehouse, scheduling the jobs that keep it current, and keeping the infrastructure in code.
        </p>
        <p>
          The interesting problems are the ones a diagram leaves out. What happens when a job restarts halfway? When the
          same change arrives twice, or a delete never arrives? And how do you show that the numbers at the end are right?
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="path">
        <h2 id="path">How I got here</h2>
        <p>
          I started on the analysis side, in market research and then as a data analyst, writing Python to automate the
          reporting I was asked for. I moved into building the platforms underneath that reporting, and I've worked as a
          data engineer since 2023. I studied for an MSc in Data Science at the University of Hertfordshire.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="how">
        <h2 id="how">How I work</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>I write significant decisions down: the options, the trade-off, and why.</li>
          <li>Changes go through review, infrastructure included.</li>
          <li>Before a new pipeline replaces an old one, I reconcile its results against the source.</li>
          <li>I use AI coding agents every day, inside guardrails I built that hand risky operations back to me.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="now">
        <h2 id="now">What I'm exploring now</h2>
        <p>
          How AI agents change the way data pipelines are operated: what they can safely be allowed to do on their own,
          and what should still need a person to approve.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="tools">
        <h2 id="tools">Tools I use</h2>
        <p>
          Snowflake and dbt for the warehouse; Airflow and Dagster for orchestration; Terraform for warehouse
          infrastructure; AWS services such as S3, Lambda and DMS; Python and SQL throughout.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="about-c__connect">
        <a class="text-link" href={LINKS.linkedin.href} rel="me">Connect on LinkedIn</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
        <a class="text-link" href={LINKS.github.href} rel="me">GitHub</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
        <a class="text-link" href={url('/concepts/architecture/')}>Read the architecture library</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</ConceptLayout>

<style>
  .about-c {
    padding-block: var(--s-8) var(--s-6);
  }

  .about-c__head h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 1.4rem + 3vw, 4rem);
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-4);
  }

  .about-c__head .lede {
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  .about-c__body {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-top: var(--s-6);
  }

  .about-c__body h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin: var(--s-7) 0 var(--s-3);
  }

  .about-c__body li + li {
    margin-top: var(--s-2);
  }

  .about-c__connect {
    margin-top: var(--s-7);
  }
</style>
